 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The damsel of the Isaurian mountain\nHer youth is golden, and her youth appears\nThe first bliss to all by education born;\nBut she with a trembling tenderness,\nLike some unmarred sunbeam slipping\nFrom the soft and dim vault of heaven,\nDown where'er it passes, through darkness,\nWith the light that falls on human eyes,\nTears are seen - and tears for life remain;\nBut as the brighter regions appear,\n'Tis known upon her brow there shines again,\nNot one tear remains - long let forever",
